From 5d0c810b0ba8c2cf747f73d75d0164ffc72de5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: clover porter <clover@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:44:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: mmcc-sdm660: do not keep video_core_clk_src always
 on

video_core_clk_src is marked CLK_IS_CRITICAL. An RCG has no gate of its
own, so the flag's only effect is a permanent enable on its parent, the
RPM XO clock (bi_tcxo), which is voted in both the active and the sleep
set. Linux therefore always asks the RPM to keep XO on while the CPUs
sleep, and the SoC can never enter XO shutdown (vlow/vmin).

On clover, a clk trace across s2idle shows every other bi_tcxo user (the
display vsync and AHB clocks) dropping its vote, while bi_tcxo itself is
never disabled; the RPM master stats show APSS shutdowns but no APSS XO
shutdown.

The Venus driver enables video_core_clk (and with it this RCG) whenever
it uses the hardware, so the RCG need not be pinned otherwise.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-sdm660.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-sdm660.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-sdm660.c
index dbd3f561d..65162cb41 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-sdm660.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-sdm660.c
@@ -1087,7 +1087,6 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 video_core_clk_src = {
 		.parent_data = mmcc_xo_mmpll0_mmpll8_mmpll3_mmpll6_gpll0_mmpll7,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(mmcc_xo_mmpll0_mmpll8_mmpll3_mmpll6_gpll0_mmpll7),
 		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
-		.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 	},
 };
 
